All code in this directory is our own. The protocol it speaks was learned from these sources:

  alphabin/ClaudeWyze4Sln (MIT, "Copyright (c) 2026 ClaudeWyze4Sln contributors"), commit 8e63ae0
    https://github.com/alphabin/ClaudeWyze4Sln  - WRITEUP.md, lake/provision.py, v4-quickstream/www/lake.html
    (the Wyze web viewer's get-streams / create-connection / renew-token calls, the signature2 scheme and
    constants, the XXTEA wrapping of the media key and salt, the sight-safe::check-user wake-up command,
    camera::resolution values)
  Jezza34000/homeassistant_petkit (MIT, "Copyright (c) 2024 - 2026 @Jezza34000"), commit 4a474a5
    https://github.com/Jezza34000/homeassistant_petkit  - custom_components/petkit/agora_api.py, agora_websocket.py,
    agora_sdp.py (Agora's web access point request/response, the gateway WebSocket, join_v3, ORTC <-> SDP)
  Agora Web SDK NG 4.24.0 (agora-rtc-sdk-ng, AgoraRTC_N-production.js), read only, not redistributed: field names,
    defaults, the data_stream envelope, the ping cadence, and the RSA public key (Agora's) that wraps the media secret.

  IDisposable/docker-wyze-bridge PR #161 (t0nyz0) is AGPL-3.0. It was read to understand the protocol and its field
  measurements (HEVC-only stream, 4096-packet SRTP window, receive buffers, renewal at 2/3 of the token life); no code
  from it was copied.

